@startuml tls13_handshake
!theme cyborg
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam backgroundColor #0b1018
skinparam defaultFontColor #e6edf7
skinparam ArrowColor #a9b8ca
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
title Generic TLS 1.3 full handshake with server-only authentication (RFC 8446 sec. 2, Figure 1)
participant Client
participant Server
Client -> Server : ClientHello: supported_versions, key_share,\nsignature_algorithms (sec. 4.1.2)
Server -> Client : ServerHello: selected version, key_share (sec. 4.1.3)
note over Client, Server : handshake keys derived; following messages encrypted
Server -> Client : {EncryptedExtensions} (sec. 4.3.1)
Server -> Client : {Certificate}: server certificate chain (sec. 4.4.2)
Server -> Client : {CertificateVerify}: signature over the transcript (sec. 4.4.3)
Server -> Client : {Finished}: MAC over the transcript (sec. 4.4.4)
Client -> Client : verify certificate, CertificateVerify and Finished
Client -> Server : {Finished} (sec. 4.4.4)
note over Client, Server : application traffic keys; [Application Data] in both directions (sec. 2)
Client <-> Server : [Application Data]
note over Client, Server
 Without CertificateRequest the client sends no Certificate: only the server is authenticated.
 A connection can carry several requests; a new request needs no new handshake.
end note
@enduml
